le author names, separate individuals with a ; (semicolon). Example: Jin, D S; Ye, J\nL86:   * Author names enclosed in quotes will return only exact matches. For example, \"Stephen Hawking\" will not return matches for Stephen W. Hawking.\nL87:   * Diacritic character variants are automatically searched in the Author(s) field.\nL88:   * Queries with no punctuation will treat each term independently.\nL89: #### Searching by subcategory\nL90: \nL91:   * To search within a subcategory select All fields.\nL92:   * A subcategory search can be combined with an author or keyword search by clicking on add another term in advanced search.\nL93: ## Tips\nL94: \nL95: Wildcards:\nL96: \nL97:   * Use ? to replace a single character or * to replace any number of characters.\nL98:   * Can be used in any field, but not in the first character position. See Journal References tips for exceptions.\nL99: \nL100: Expressions:\nL101: \nL102:   * TeX expressions can be searched, enclosed in single $ characters.\nL103: \nL104: Phrases:\nL105: \nL106:   * Enclose phrases in double quotes for exact matches in title, abstract, and comments.\nL107: \nL108: Dates:\nL109:   * Sorting by announcement date will use the year and month the original version (v1) of the paper was announced.\nL110:   * Sorting by submission date will use the year, month and day the latest version of the paper was submitted.\nL111: \nL112: Journal References:\nL113:   * If a journal reference search contains a wildcard, matches will be made using wildcard matching as expected. For example, math* will match math, maths, mathematics.\nL114:   * If a journal reference search does not contain a wildcard, only exact phrases entered will be matched. For example, math would match math or math and science but not maths or mathematics.\nL115:   * All journal reference searches that do not contain a wildcard are literal searches: a search for Physica A will match all papers with journal references containing Physica A, but a search for Physica A, 245 (1997) 181 will only return the paper with journal reference Physica A, 245 (1997) 181.\nL116: cite6†Search v0.5.6 released 2020-02-24†github.com L117: \nL118: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite8†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL119: \nL120: cite9†About†info.arxiv.org · cite10†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite11†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite12†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite13†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite14†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite15†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite16†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L121: \nL122: Major funding support from\n"
